.SS "int libusb_alloc_streams (\fBlibusb_device_handle\fP * dev_handle, uint32_t num_streams, unsigned char * endpoints, int num_endpoints)"

.PP
Allocate up to num_streams usb bulk streams on the specified endpoints\&. This function takes an array of endpoints rather then a single endpoint because some protocols require that endpoints are setup with similar stream ids\&. All endpoints passed in must belong to the same interface\&.

.PP
Note this function may return less streams then requested\&. Also note that the same number of streams are allocated for each endpoint in the endpoint array\&.

.PP
Stream id 0 is reserved, and should not be used to communicate with devices\&. If \fBlibusb_alloc_streams()\fP returns with a value of N, you may use stream ids 1 to N\&.

.PP
Since version 1\&.0\&.19, \fBLIBUSB_API_VERSION\fP >= 0x01000103

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdev_handle\fP a device handle 
.br
\fInum_streams\fP number of streams to try to allocate 
.br
\fIendpoints\fP array of endpoints to allocate streams on 
.br
\fInum_endpoints\fP length of the endpoints array 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
number of streams allocated, or a LIBUSB_ERROR code on failure 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int libusb_free_streams (\fBlibusb_device_handle\fP * dev_handle, unsigned char * endpoints, int num_endpoints)"

.PP
