.SS "void libusb_fill_control_transfer (struct \fBlibusb_transfer\fP * transfer, \fBlibusb_device_handle\fP * dev_handle, unsigned char * buffer, \fBlibusb_transfer_cb_fn\fP callback, void * user_data, unsigned int timeout)\fR [inline]\fP, \fR [static]\fP"

.PP
Helper function to populate the required \fBlibusb_transfer\fP fields for a control transfer\&. If you pass a transfer buffer to this function, the first 8 bytes will be interpreted as a control setup packet, and the wLength field will be used to automatically populate the \fBlength\fP field of the transfer\&. Therefore the recommended approach is:
.IP "1." 4
Allocate a suitably sized data buffer (including space for control setup)
.IP "2." 4
Call \fBlibusb_fill_control_setup()\fP
.IP "3." 4
If this is a host-to-device transfer with a data stage, put the data in place after the setup packet
.IP "4." 4
Call this function
.IP "5." 4
Call \fBlibusb_submit_transfer()\fP
.PP

.PP
It is also legal to pass a NULL buffer to this function, in which case this function will not attempt to populate the length field\&. Remember that you must then populate the buffer and length fields later\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItransfer\fP the transfer to populate 
.br
\fIdev_handle\fP handle of the device that will handle the transfer 
.br
\fIbuffer\fP data buffer\&. If provided, this function will interpret the first 8 bytes as a setup packet and infer the transfer length from that\&. This pointer must be aligned to at least 2 bytes boundary\&. 
.br
\fIcallback\fP callback function to be invoked on transfer completion 
.br
\fIuser_data\fP user data to pass to callback function 
.br
\fItimeout\fP timeout for the transfer in milliseconds 
.RE
.PP

