.SS "unsigned char * libusb_get_iso_packet_buffer_simple (struct \fBlibusb_transfer\fP * transfer, unsigned int packet)\fR [inline]\fP, \fR [static]\fP"

.PP
Convenience function to locate the position of an isochronous packet within the buffer of an isochronous transfer, for transfers where each packet is of identical size\&. This function relies on the assumption that every packet within the transfer is of identical size to the first packet\&. Calculating the location of the packet buffer is then just a simple calculation: \fRbuffer + (packet_size * packet)\fP

.PP
Do not use this function on transfers other than those that have identical packet lengths for each packet\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItransfer\fP a transfer 
.br
\fIpacket\fP the packet to return the address of 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
the base address of the packet buffer inside the transfer buffer, or NULL if the packet does not exist\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
